{%- comment -%}
  Language Switcher

  The switcher visitors see: a globe button that opens a list of every language
  the site is published in. Distinct from the floating locale switcher the
  CloudCannon Connector draws inside the Visual Editor, which is editor-only and
  never reaches the built site.

  Renders nothing unless Rosey is enabled and at least one locale is configured
  under `languages` in /rosey.yml.

  Params:
    color_group  the colour group of the surface it sits on (the nav's), used
                 for the icons and the dropdown panel

  Each language is listed by its native name ("Español", "Deutsch") via the
  `languageName` filter, so a visitor can find their language whichever one the
  page is currently in. Those names are deliberately NOT Rosey-tagged: a
  language's own name must read the same in every locale.

  The original language is served from the site root because utils/rosey.js
  builds with --default-language-at-root, so its link is page.url unprefixed.
  Which language that IS comes from rosey.yml's `default_language` — it is not
  assumed to be English.

  Every link carries data-rosey-ignore. Rosey rewrites root-relative hrefs to the
  current locale when it builds each locale's copy of the site; without the
  ignore, each link would be rewritten to point at the locale you are already in
  and the switcher would do nothing.

  Rosey builds every locale from this same HTML, so which language the page is in
  is only known in the browser, from <html lang> (Rosey sets it per locale). The
  `init` handler reads it to fill in the button's language code and mark the
  current entry with aria-current. Without JS the button shows just the globe,
  and the dropdown still opens — <details> needs no script.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if rosey.enabled and rosey.languages.size > 0 -%}
  <details
    class="c-languageSwitcher group relative text-sm"
    _="init
         set current to document.documentElement.lang
         repeat for link in <a[hreflang]/> in me
           if link.getAttribute('hreflang') is current
             call link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true')
             put current into the first <.c-languageSwitcher__current/> in me
           end
         end
       end
       on click from elsewhere remove @open from me end
       on keydown[key is 'Escape']
         if I match <[open]/>
           remove @open from me
           set trigger to the first <summary/> in me
           call trigger.focus()
         end
       end"
  >
    <summary
      class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-1.5 {{ theme.button_rounding }} border border-{{ color_group }}-textcolor border-opacity-30 px-2.5 py-1.5 transition-colors hover:border-opacity-70 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"
      aria-label="Language"{{ "Language" | roseyAttrs: "aria-label", "ui:language" }}
    >
      {% bookshop "generic/heroLibraryIcon" heroLibraryIconName: "globe-alt" iconType: "outline" iconSize: 'micro' roundedBorder: false themeColor: true color_group: color_group %}
      {%- comment -%}Globe only on small screens, so the header's button row still
      fits beside the logo and the menu toggle doesn't wrap onto its own line.{%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="c-languageSwitcher__current hidden min-w-[2ch] font-medium uppercase sm:inline" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hidden transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 sm:inline-flex" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- bookshop "generic/heroLibraryIcon" heroLibraryIconName: "chevron-down" iconType: "outline" iconSize: 'micro' roundedBorder: false themeColor: true color_group: color_group -%}
      </span>
    </summary>

    <ul class="absolute right-0 top-full z-10 mt-2 min-w-[11rem] overflow-hidden py-1 {{ theme.container_rounding }} border border-{{ color_group }}-textcolor border-opacity-20 bg-{{ color_group }}-backgroundcolor bg-opacity-95 text-{{ color_group }}-textcolor shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
      {%- for locale in rosey.allLanguages -%}
        <li>
          <a
            href="{% if locale == rosey.defaultLanguage %}{{ page.url }}{% else %}/{{ locale }}{{ page.url }}{% endif %}"
            data-rosey-ignore
            hreflang="{{ locale }}"
            lang="{{ locale }}"
            class="group/lang flex items-center justify-between gap-4 whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-2 hover:underline aria-[current=true]:font-semibold"
          >
            <span>{{ locale | languageName }}</span>
            <span class="invisible group-aria-[current=true]/lang:visible" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- bookshop "generic/heroLibraryIcon" heroLibraryIconName: "check" iconType: "outline" iconSize: 'micro' roundedBorder: false themeColor: true color_group: color_group -%}
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </details>
{%- endif -%}
